# Test: ze config validate asks the running ze about an external plugin's section
#
# Question: with a ze running that started an external plugin, does the local
# `ze config validate <file>`, on a file in the operator's working directory,
# get that file judged by the running ze: a section under the plugin's own root
# accepted with the output of a local acceptance, and a value outside the
# range the plugin's module declares refused with exit 1?
# Why not a unit test: TestValidateRouteDrawsTheDaemonsAcceptance and
# TestValidateRouteDrawsTheDaemonsRefusal prove the route over a stub ask. Only
# two processes show that the file's content reaches the daemon over SSH, that
# the daemon judges it with the schema it read from the plugin at start, and
# that a refused config still carries its diagnostics back on the exec channel.
#
# What proves the daemon answered: this process holds no schema of acme-monitor
# (ze starts no external plugin with no daemon), so alone it refuses the
# section as an unknown keyword. Acceptance, and a refusal that names the
# range, can only come from the ze that ran the plugin.
#
# The files are in the test's working directory, which the daemon route never
# reads by path (command.CallerPath admits its config directories only): the
# content travels in the command.
#
# VALIDATES: the phase "ze config validate asks the running ze" of
#   spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup: acceptance, range refusal, exit codes.
# PREVENTS: "not available" from the local command while a ze that can judge
#   the section runs; a daemon refusal that arrives with no diagnostics.

option=timeout:value=90s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.username:value=admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT

tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_RUNNING
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
plugin {
	external acme-monitor {
		run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang valid"
		encoder json
	}
}

acme-monitor {
	target probe-a
	interval 5
}
EOF_RUNNING

tmpfs=good.conf:terminator=EOF_GOOD
plugin {
	external acme-monitor {
		run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang valid"
		encoder json
	}
}

acme-monitor {
	target probe-b
	interval 7
}
EOF_GOOD

# refused=config-yang-range declares the body a config Ze must refuse, for the
# repository config sweep (TestRepositoryConfigsValidate).
tmpfs=bad.conf:refused=config-yang-range:terminator=EOF_BAD
plugin {
	external acme-monitor {
		run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang valid"
		encoder json
	}
}

acme-monitor {
	target probe-b
	interval 11
}
EOF_BAD

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start running.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.
expect=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: external-yang configure root=acme-monitor leaves=[acme-monitor/interval=5 acme-monitor/target=probe-a]

# The running ze judges the section and accepts it; the local command prints
# the line a local acceptance prints.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate good.conf:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid: good.conf
reject=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword
reject=stdout:contains=none answered

# The running ze refuses the value with the plugin's own range, and the local
# command prints the refusal and exits 1.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate bad.conf:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=configuration invalid: bad.conf
expect=stdout:contains=is outside the accepted range
expect=stdout:contains=interval accepts a value in
reject=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword
reject=stdout:contains=none answered
